# The OVRTX image consumes only the package source, constraints, legal files,
# and its own service subtree. Default-deny everything else so local daemon
# state, credentials, examples, LFS assets, and benchmark outputs never enter
# the Docker build context.
**
!.dockerignore
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!requirements/
!requirements/constraints.txt
!src/
!src/**
!apps/
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/LICENSE
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/README.md
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/docker-entrypoint.sh
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/pyproject.toml
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/service/
!apps/ovrtx_rendering_api/service/**

# Re-exclude generated native/Python artifacts if they exist under an allowed
# source directory in a developer checkout.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.pyd
**/*.dylib
